gb_gatekeeper (android.hardware.gatekeeper-service.gb)
Software Gatekeeper HAL for Googlebook OS on VMware and on the Surface Book 3.

Our own code (src/, tests/, tools/, build.sh, rc/, vintf/, component/): Apache-2.0, see the
repository LICENSE.

This directory and the binary built from it also contain:

1. AOSP libgatekeeper, unmodified
   third_party/aosp/system_gatekeeper/  (gatekeeper.cpp, gatekeeper_messages.cpp,
   include/gatekeeper/*.h)
   https://android.googlesource.com/platform/system/gatekeeper  branch android17-release,
   commit 5b5e75b5bda9fccbc3132e9624cb25286babdaac
   Copyright (C) 2015 The Android Open Source Project. Licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0.

2. AOSP hw_auth_token.h, unmodified
   third_party/aosp/libhardware/include/hardware/hw_auth_token.h
   https://android.googlesource.com/platform/hardware/libhardware  (include_all/hardware/)
   branch android17-release, commit 97ee3e33ec5ba48c0eca8341ed377ac4497a0678
   Copyright (C) 2014 The Android Open Source Project. Licensed under the Apache License,
   Version 2.0.

3. AOSP libbinder_ndk platform headers, unmodified, used only by the compile-time ABI check
   (src/abi_check.cpp); not part of the binary
   third_party/aosp/libbinder_ndk_platform/android/  (binder_manager.h, binder_process.h,
   binder_stability.h)
   https://android.googlesource.com/platform/frameworks/native  (libs/binder/ndk/include_platform/)
   branch android17-release, commit ae266dcb706d083868578cfedce381ef44488a07.
   Copyright The Android Open Source Project. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

4. BoringSSL (libcrypto, linked statically; not stored here, fetched by build.sh)
   https://android.googlesource.com/platform/external/boringssl  branch android17-release,
   commit 0cd1f6a94b670e6b61af95a06e71e690ae8e3262
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (its LICENSE; the Go-licensed test-suite code
   it mentions is not part of libcrypto). The full text is copied next to the binary as
   out/android/licenses/LICENSE.boringssl.

5. Design references (behaviour reproduced, code not copied unless stated)
   * AOSP nonsecure Gatekeeper, hardware/interfaces/gatekeeper/aidl/software (Apache-2.0):
     the scrypt parameters of the password signature, the ISharedSecret participant and the
     AIDL error mapping.
   * AOSP system/keymaster km_openssl/soft_keymaster_enforcement.cpp and ckdf.cpp
     (Apache-2.0): the shared HMAC key derivation (CKDF, zero agreement key, labels).

6. gbOS86 software Gatekeeper
   gatekeeper/soft_gk.c of gbOS86, https://github.com/linuxkid473/gbos-x86 , commit 03a6a46,
   by Vihaan Nathan, "SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0".
   The idea of a hand-written stable-AIDL server over the libbinder_ndk C API, its parcelable
   framing (non-null marker + size patched afterwards) and the meta-transaction codes are
   adapted from it in src/aidl_service.cpp and src/binder_api.h. Its fixed compile-time keys,
   its self-signed auth tokens and its missing throttling were not taken over.

The NDK's libc++ (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception) is linked statically.
